This case is to Setup kdump to a NFS target.

* Summary of these optional parameters:
CRASHSIZE: custom kdump crashsize support
NFSSERVER: nfs server for saving dumps.
VMCOREPATH: nfs server export.
WEBSERVERBASEURL: base URL for the web server the dumps will be available at.
NO_COMPRESS: any positive integer(usually 1) explicitly іndicating the dump file
must be of uncompressed ELF format. Otherwise, omitting this param or 0 for the
compressed format.
COMPRESSION: choose zlib or lzo compression algorithm.  zlib is default on RHEL6 and older; lzo is default on RHEL7 and newer.  NO_COMPRESS overrides this parameter.
UPGRADE_FC_KDUMP:
	default: false
	When it's true and it's testing on Fedora, it will try upgrading
	kexec-tools/dracut/systemd to the latest versions on Rawhide.
